d 'MCSET': module to construct the Model Confidence Set (MCS)
d
d	 The mcset command implements the Model Confidence Set
d (MCS) procedure of Hansen, Lunde,    and Nason (2011), which
d provides a formal way to ask which forecasting models are   
d statistically distinguishable from the best-performing
d alternatives. The main output of    the procedure is not a single
d “winner”, but a set of models that cannot be rejected as	 
d having superior predictive ability at a chosen confidence level.
d The algorithm is based    on the implementation in R provided by
d Catania (2026), first described by Bernardi and    Catania (2014)
d and the block bootstrap schemes of Baum and Otero (forthcoming). 
d
d KW: model confidence
d KW: forecasting
d KW: block bootstrap
d
d Requires: Stata version 14 
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260810
d
d Author: Christopher F Baum, Boston College 
d Support: email baum@@bc.edu
d
d Author: Jesús Otero, Universidad del Rosario
d Support: email jesus.otero@@urosario.edu.co
d
f mcset.ado
f mcset.sthlp
